                <head>256. National Security Council Report<anchor n="1" xml:id="d256-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">Supplement to NSC 5718</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic">August 5,
                        1957</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">MEMORANDUM FOR THE NATIONAL SECURITY COUNCIL</p>
                <p>The National Security Council, the Secretary of the Treasury, and the Director,
                    Bureau of the Budget, at the 333rd Council meeting on August 1, 1957 (NSC Action
                    No. 1763):</p>
                <p>[Here follows NSC Action No. 1763; for text, see <ref target="#d253-f3">footnote
                        3, Document 253</ref>.]</p>
                <p>The President has this date approved the above actions. Accordingly, the enclosed
                    revised page 2 of the Supplement to NSC 5718, incorporating the amendment
                    referred to in b above, is transmitted herewith for insertion in all copies,
                    with the request that the superseded page be destroyed by burning, in accordance
                    with security regulations.</p>
                <p>In accordance with c above, the Supplement to NSC 5718 is being referred to the
                    Secretary of State for his use in the conduct of future U.S. foreign relations
                    with respect to the Cyprus dispute.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">S. Everett Gleason</hi><lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Executive Secretary</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d256-a1.xml" xpointer="d256-a1"/>
